{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe MCP gate singleflight key (`src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py` `compute_key`) hashes gate,\ncanonical ticket id, code basis SHA, variant, and readonly flag. Both completion call sites in\n`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` pass `variant=f\"graph={graph};source={source or 'attested'}\"`:\n`verify_completion_start` (~line 313) and the sync `verify_completion` tool (~line 420). The\nticket's text is not in the key. So while a completion check of ticket T is in flight, editing T\nand starting another check returns the SAME run, which read the old text when it started.\n\nThis is the same mechanism fixed for plan review in next-embattled-geese (3b27-8f4b, Gerrit\n3040), which added the material fingerprint via `_plan_review_variant`.\n\nHarm is worse than for plan review. Plan review re-checks its material under the store lock\nbefore signing; completion does not (bug daredevil-marginal-dodo, 0521-7e68). The attached\npre-edit run signs a PASS whose manifest binds the POST-edit material, and a close then reuses\nit. Dedup therefore routes the author's correct \"edit, then re-verify\" into that hole: they\nreceive a signed PASS for text that was never verified. This ticket stops the re-verify from\nattaching; daredevil-marginal-dodo fixes what the attached run signs. Both are needed; this one\ndoes not depend on the other.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Add `_completion_variant(ticket_id, graph, source)` in `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` returning\n   `f\"graph={graph};source={source or 'attested'};material={fp}\"`, with `fp` from\n   `rebar.llm.plan_review.attest.current_material_fingerprint(ticket_id)` (light read, no LLM).\n2. Use it at both completion call sites. In `verify_completion_start` compute it inside the\n   worker thread (same as `review_plan_start`), not on the event loop.\n3. `material=None` arm: `current_material_fingerprint_impl` returns None on a read failure,\n   and RE-RAISES a pinned ticket-view failure. A shared `_material_key` catches a raising read\n   and returns None, so a gate start never fails on its own dedup key; the gate still runs and\n   reports the read failure. `_plan_review_variant` (3040) uses the same helper: on\n   82a91a89f1d a raising read escapes it and fails the tool call before the gate starts. None\n   keys dedup only with each other, never with a run keyed on a real fingerprint.\n4. `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py::test_verify_completion_start_preserves_graph_tristate_and_variant_key`\n   pins the literal old variant `graph=None;source=attested`. Its purpose (graph tri-state kept,\n   start and sync share one key) is unchanged; only the expected literal gains\n   `;material=None` (its ticket `d80d` does not exist in that store, so the read returns None).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Test in `tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py`: a blocked `verify_completion_start` run is in\n  flight, the description is edited, a second start returns a NEW job whose gate call sees the\n  edited text. Fails on origin/main 82a91a89f1d.\n- [ ] Same through the sync `verify_completion` tool: after an edit, a concurrent call runs the\n  gate a second time. Fails on origin/main.\n- [ ] Unchanged material still dedups: the existing\n  `test_two_concurrent_calls_invoke_the_gate_exactly_once[verify_completion]` passes unchanged.\n- [ ] Key-shape test, for both the completion and plan-review variants: different fingerprints\n  give different variants; a None fingerprint AND a raising read both give the\n  `...;material=None` variant, distinct from both. The raising-read case fails on 82a91a89f1d.\n- [ ] The graph tri-state test still asserts start/sync key parity, with the updated literal.\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py -p no:randomly -q\nmake lint && make typecheck && make verify\n```"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792380299926133001,"uuid":"16daf18c-0299-4450-b26f-700b9674ff3a"}